mqtt-monitor (1.1.0-0rc8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Introduce the V2 runtime with inventory discovery for disks, RAID, mounts, and LXC.
  * Add a first-class issue engine with active and resolved transitions.
  * Publish Home Assistant issue and container entities plus a generated dashboard.
  * Add optional Home Assistant notifications and package the runtime state directory.
  * Compare package versions before self-updating so RC builds do not downgrade to latest stable.
  * Sanitize Home Assistant entity prefixes and skip noisy LXC bind mounts in filesystem discovery.
  * Retry non-NVMe SMART probes across device modes and parse SCSI SMART health correctly.
  * Include mapper-backed monitored mounts in disk discovery and expose logical multipath volumes.
  * Sanitize disk entity IDs so names such as mpatha-part1 produce valid Home Assistant entities.
  * Hide unsupported SMART-only rows from generated dashboard cards for logical volumes.
  * Redesign the generated Home Assistant dashboard into a sections-based operational view.
  * Sanitize filesystem, RAID, container, and issue slugs used in Home Assistant entities.
  * Sync the live Home Assistant monitor view from the generated dashboard source of truth.
  * Declare python3-yaml as a package dependency for dashboard generation.
  * Discover classic-LXC system containers through a narrow privileged helper instead of user-scoped lxc-ls access.
  * Package the helper, install a single-command sudoers rule, and keep the monitor itself unprivileged.

 -- Joao Lino <joao.oliveira.lino@gmail.com> Sun, 12 Apr 2026 17:25:00 +0200

mqtt-monitor (1.0.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Grant the service the Linux capabilities needed for NVMe SMART reads.
  * Keep the dedicated service account instead of falling back to root.

 -- Joao Lino <joao.oliveira.lino@gmail.com> Sun, 12 Apr 2026 13:50:00 +0200

mqtt-monitor (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix SMART capacity caching so the service no longer crashes on restart.
  * Publish delta-based disk I/O metrics to avoid bogus startup spikes.
  * Keep valid NVMe SMART data online even when smartctl sets warning bits.
  * Publish retained MQTT discovery/state payloads for the current Home Assistant schema.
  * Fix RAID failed-device parsing and add broader loop error handling.

 -- Joao Lino <joao.oliveira.lino@gmail.com> Sun, 12 Apr 2026 13:30:00 +0200

mqtt-monitor (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of MQTT Monitor.
  * Monitors disk SMART attributes, RAID status, and system metrics.
  * Publishes to MQTT for Home Assistant integration.
  * Supports automatic version updates via GitHub Releases.
  * Includes log rotation and configuration preservation.

